{"search_note":"I found no direct evidence that 2024 military spending was used to enrich a patronage network or directly reward security elites.

I also found no transparent breakdown proving the defense buildup was proportionate to battlefield need rather than political signaling.

The public record supports a mixed reading: real security need was present, but Tshisekedi also used mobilization to project strength and pressure neighbors.","evidence":[{"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo: 2024 Article IV Consultation, Sixth Review Under the Extended Credit Facility Arrangement, Request for a Waiver of Nonobservance of Quantitative Performance Criterion, and Financing Assurances Review-Press Release; Staff Report; and Statement by the Executive Director for Democratic Republic of the Congo","publisher":"IMF","date":"2024-07-15","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/cr/issues/2024/07/15/democratic-republic-of-the-congo-2024-article-iv-consultation-sixth-review-under-the-551892","summary":"The IMF said the 2024 fiscal deficit was being eased partly by higher mining revenue, while “higher security spending” was pressuring the budget because of escalating conflict in the east and the gradual UN force withdrawal. This is the strongest evidence that spending increases were tied to real security needs.","question_ids":["2B.8","2B.3","1B.3"]},{"title":"Congolese president sacks military top brass in major reshuffle","publisher":"Reuters","date":"2024-12-20","url":"https://theprint.in/world/congolese-president-sacks-military-top-brass-in-major-reshuffle/2411531/","summary":"Reuters reported Tshisekedi replaced the armed forces chief, military intelligence head, and many senior officers in one of the biggest reshuffles in years. The report notes his office had previously described defense reforms as aimed at “boosting efficiency.” This is compatible with legitimate restructuring, but it can also be read as elite management and strength projection.","question_ids":["2B.8","1B.7","1B.3"]},{"title":"Face à la presse, le Président Félix Tshisekedi a peint un tableau d’espoir de la RDC","publisher":"Présidence RDC","date":"2024-02-23","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/face_a_la_presse_le_president_felix_tshisekedi_a_peint_un_tableau_despoir_de_la_rdc","summary":"Tshisekedi emphasized a major military buildup and a force-forward approach to the eastern security problem. That suggests mobilization and military spending were also being used to project strength and pressure opponents, not only to meet narrow defensive needs.","question_ids":["2B.8","2B.3","1B.3","1B.7"]},{"title":"Army disarray hobbles Congo's fight with Rwanda-backed rebels, officers say","publisher":"Reuters","date":"2024-07-04","url":"https://d2233.cms.socastsrm.com/2024/07/04/army-disarray-hobbles-congos-fight-with-rwanda-backed-rebels-officers-say/","summary":"Reuters reported Tshisekedi threatened to declare war against Rwanda and described the army’s reliance on pro-government militias such as Wazalendo. This is the clearest evidence that mobilization was used in an intimidation/projection posture and through proxy structures, not purely as measured defense.","question_ids":["2B.8","2B.3","2B.2","1B.6","1B.7","1B.3"]},{"title":"Army disarray hobbles Congo's fight with Rwanda-backed rebels, sources say","publisher":"Reuters","date":"2024-06-27","url":"https://www.reutersconnect.com/item/army-disarray-hobbles-congos-fight-with-rwanda-backed-rebels-sources-say/dGFnOnJldXRlcnMuY29tLDIwMjQ6bmV3c21sX0xWQTAwODUzODEwMjA3MjAyNFJQMQ","summary":"Reuters described the Congolese response as a coalition of army forces, Burundian troops, South African forces, and Wazalendo militias, underscoring that mobilization was broad, improvised, and difficult to coordinate. That supports the view that spending and mobilization were driven by battlefield necessity, but also that they were messy and proxy-heavy.","question_ids":["2B.8","1B.6","1B.7","1B.3"]},{"title":"Programme de désarmement et démobilisation : une alternative pour la paix et la cohésion sociale","publisher":"ACP","date":"2024-03-22","url":"https://acp.cd/nation/programme-de-desarmement-et-demobilisation-une-alternative-pour-la-paix-et-la-cohesion-sociale/","summary":"The government described P-DDRCS as a stabilization and cohesion program to restore state authority where absent. This is not military spending, but it is relevant evidence that part of the state’s security effort was framed as disarmament and demobilization rather than pure force projection.","question_ids":["2B.8","1B.6","1B.4"]}]}
